Audio clips that play past their edges, and a host fade node (Segno: docs/design/fades.md, ADR 0036).

Segno's crossfades sit at the join between two clips that meet without overlapping: while one lasts,
each clip plays some of its source past its edge. EngineBehaviour::getAudioClipExtension lets the
host extend the range an audio clip's node plays (its source offset moved to match, and the track's
scheduling widened through getHead/getTail), and createAudioClipFadeNode lets it apply the clip's fades
with its own node over that range. With neither overridden, nothing changes.

